; ecosystem-status.my — machine-readable current-state snapshot for the
; four-repository ecosystem (my-lisp, fpga-lisp, cml, my-idea).
;
; Data only, same convention as language-contract.my/isa-contract.my/
; compatibility.my — one flat alist, read via (read-file ...) or (read
; (read-file "ecosystem-status.my")), never loaded as executable source.
; docs/ecosystem-sync.md's prose narrates the same facts for humans;
; this file is the version another session's my-lisp code could actually
; consume (e.g. a future my-idea "System Observatory" panel) without
; scraping Markdown.
;
; Not the contract itself — language-contract.my/isa-contract.my/
; compatibility.my remain authoritative; this file is a snapshot,
; refreshed by hand after each cross-session sync, per
; docs/ecosystem-sync.md's four-point status request.
;
; ecosystem-status.my — машинно-читаний знімок поточного стану
; чотирьох-репозиторної екосистеми. Дані, не код; та сама конвенція, що
; й у language-contract.my/isa-contract.my/compatibility.my.

((kind . ecosystem-status)
 (as-of . "2026-08-11")
 (repositories .
  ((my-lisp .
    ((role . semantic-source-of-truth)
     (language-contract . (1 0))
     (exactness-model . fully-implemented)
     (blocking-others . nil)
     (rust-toolchain-on-this-machine . (installed 1 97 1))
     (msvc-linker-status . working-after-disk-freed)
     (gnu-toolchain-status . flaky-shared-rustup-default-with-cml-use-msvc-instead)
     (tcp-repl . (flag "--tcp[=PORT]" commit "1a9dd63" bind "127.0.0.1-only"
                   isolation-fix "c762a0c" logging "8c1631a"
                   note "each connection gets its own fresh Environment::root(), not a shared mutable Session — a connection's def is invisible to every other connection; every expression logged to stderr with peer address"))))
   (fpga-lisp .
    ((role . hardware-implementation)
     (isa-contract . (0 2))
     (hardware-verified-milestones . (m01 . m27))
     (m28-status . passed-real-iverilog-run)
     (m28-commit . "447ee0e")
     (m28-fix-commit . "7542682")
     (m29-status . passed-real-iverilog-run)
     (m29-commit . "cec7889")
     (m29-note . "canonical tail-recursive length/length-onto — bootstraps reverse/append/map from core.my")
     (m28-m29-root-cause . "not the letrec/SETCDR mechanism — that worked correctly from the start. The two demo files' test data (a b c) was passed unquoted into a call position, so it was evaluated as code: 'a looked up as an operator, unbound lookup fell through to NIL, CAR(NIL) hit a type error, and halted with garbage registers — which read as the wrong result (a stray symbol) and was first misdiagnosed as a call-stack imbalance bug. Every earlier bootstrap demo had correctly quoted its test data; these two didn't. Fixed by quoting '(a b c) in both files. Re-run confirmed: M28 PASSED (sim time 115224960), M29 PASSED (sim time 121180340), R9=TAG:FIXNUM VAL:3 in both.")
     (ci-commit . "9e9ea06")
     (ci-status . green)
     (conformance-my-running . nil)
     (open-blocker . nil)
     (open-blocker-note . "letrec-in-closures (plan item 24) resolved — M28/M29 both pass on real iverilog now that the actual bug (unquoted test data, not the mechanism) was found and fixed")
     (isa-representational-gaps . (no-inexact-numbers no-rationals no-string-tag))))
   (cml .
    ((role . aot-compiler)
     (compiler-version . (0 1 0))
     (tested-my-lisp-sha . "ed10151")
     (tested-fpga-lisp-sha . "01bb01a")
     (tier-1-fixtures . (29 . 34))
     (equal-status . known-broken-skipped-again)
     (equal-commit . "6b884a8")
     (equal-fix-commit . "4565549")
     (equal-regression-1 . "register-clobber in cons/eq/equal? — a nested call overwrote the caller's R1; fixed af64449, verified on (cons 'a 'b)")
     (equal-regression-2 . "after regression-1's fix, cml_equal itself hangs on real hardware for a trivially-equal comparison — separate, deeper, unresolved bug; equal? put back under skip, compatibility.my updated (c8476b9) to known-broken, removed from supported list")
     (equal-regression-2-jf-hypothesis-ruled-out . "my-lisp's own guess that fpga-lisp's confirmed G8/JF deviation (control.sv:147, tag==NIL || (tag==FIXNUM && value==0)) was the cause was checked and most likely wrong by fpga-lisp: every register cml_equal branches on via JF (R5/R6 ATOM results, R7 EQ result, R6 worklist-empty-check) is always a TRUE/NIL tag from EQ/ATOM, never a raw FIXNUM 0. fpga-lisp instead suspects an unbalanced call stack around CALL (same class as the M28 bug, R11), pointed cml at control.sv:350-359 for EQ and asked for an R11 dump right before CALL")
     (defmacro-status . merged-fixed-and-now-genuinely-verified)
     (defmacro-commit . "a8e6cdf")
     (tier-1-skips-remaining . 1)
     (tier-1-fixtures-passing . 24)
     (ci-status . was-falsely-reported-green-now-corrected)
     (ci-false-positive-note . "all 8 CI runs on master from 6b884a8 onward actually FAILURE — cml first checked via WebFetch on the GitHub Actions HTML page, which misreported success; installing iverilog+python3 locally and running for real failed immediately on (equal? '(p . 0) (cons 'p 0)) with UnknownSymbol; root cause was the test harness's static_error() unknown-operator table not updated when equal? was added — the compiler itself always compiled equal? correctly, only the harness's static check was wrong; fixed in 4565549, status doc corrected in 3f2c8d7. Lesson recorded ecosystem-wide: verify CI via the REST API (conclusion field on /actions/runs) not the HTML Actions page")
     (ci-created-without-user-confirmation . t)
     (compatibility-my-updated . "b2c52c2")
     (compatibility-my-note . "pipeline now includes macro-expand; supported now includes equal?/defmacro; conformance is 34 tagged tier-1, 9 skipped, all one inexact-number gap")
     (testing-docs . "docs/testing.md (218e461), trilingual, linked from README")
     (agents-md . "b347c03")
     (tcp-repl-connected . t)
     (documented-limitations . (no-inexact-numbers no-rationals no-canonical-strings
                                 no-more-than-eight-call-arguments))))
   (my-idea .
    ((role . observer-and-ide)
     (joined-ecosystem-sync . "2026-08-11")
     (depends-on-my-lisp-via . (cargo-git-dependency git-submodule))
     (revision-sync-risk . manual-only-no-ci-invariant)
     (planned-feature . system-observatory)))))
 (open-blockers .
  ((letrec-in-fpga-lisp-closures .
    "RESOLVED (7542682) — M28/M29 both PASSED on real iverilog; the letrec/SETCDR mechanism itself was correct throughout, the bug was unquoted test data in two demo files, not the mechanism")
   (no-ecosystem-ci-until-now .
    "cml's CI (created unilaterally 2026-08-11 before user confirmation arrived) was first reported green via a since-debunked HTML-page check, then found genuinely FAILURE on all 8 runs, root-caused (stale unknown-operator table in the test harness, not the compiler) and fixed in 4565549 — equal?/defmacro are now actually machine-verified, not just reported as such")
   (verify-ci-via-rest-api-not-html .
    "cml's WebFetch on github.com/.../actions misreported a failing run as success; the REST API's `conclusion` field (api.github.com/repos/.../actions/runs?head_sha=...) is the reliable source — applies to any repo in this ecosystem checking CI status, not just cml")
   (isa-no-inexact-rational-string .
    "representational gap, not an implementation gap; blocks my-lisp's stated core purpose (exact rational arithmetic) from ever reaching fpga-lisp until isa-contract.my adds tags/encoding for it")
   (m28-manual-verification-was-wrong .
    "fpga-lisp's M28 (447ee0e) was reported manually-verified-passing but its first real iverilog run returns the param symbol instead of FIXNUM 3 — a lesson that manual trace is not a substitute for the simulator, applies equally to any 'verified by inspection' claim from any repo in this ecosystem")))
 (pending-user-decisions .
  ((cml-ci-after-the-fact . "accept cml's unilateral CI creation, or have it reverted?")))
 (how-to-refresh .
  "Ask the four-point status request from docs/ecosystem-sync.md via the CCD session-management message tool, then hand-update this file's relevant repositories/open-blockers entries. Keep docs/ecosystem-sync.md and ecosystem-status.md's prose in sync with this file's facts."))
